o background service, broad indexing, credential store use, or unbounded persistence was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts coherently provide Python coding, debugging, packaging, subprocess, HTTP, and security guidance; no shipped code executes actions on install or load.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"This skill is reasonable to install if you want Python guidance. It can cause the agent to suggest commands, dependency installs, file edits, and preference storage, so review generated commands and any remembered preferences before applying them.","findings":"[P2] expected: The hidden-character finding is a BOM character shown inside an encoding example about Excel-exported files, not a hidden instruction.\n[PE3] expected: /etc/passwd appears in a path-containment warning showing how absolute path joins can escape a base directory; it is not read or requested.\n[SSRF1] expected: 169.254.169.254 is cited as an SSRF danger in HTTP/security guidance, advising validation rather than access.\n[TM1] expected: The shell=True and rm -rf text is an explicit command-injection anti-pattern example, not a command the skill tells the agent to run.\n[TM2] expected: The command-chaining marker comes from the same anti-pattern example used to explain why interpolated shell strings are unsafe.\n[TM3] expected: verify=False and world-writable are discussed as unsafe defaults to avoid, not defaults the skill configures.\n[SQP-2] expected: Subprocess guidance is expected for a Python skill; while an upfront host-impact warning could be clearer, the file repeatedly recommends safe subprocess practices.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789056167776}}}}}